From 283d4a21cbec33855c7ee3bf784be9ed7071dd93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Catanzaro <mcatanzaro@gnome.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Feb 2026 14:48:47 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 09/50] tests: Remove file database incorrect root test

This test is failing with modern Fedora crypto policy because at least
one of the certificates are old and crufty; notably, it uses MD2, which
is apparently a thing that exists.

The test is functionally very similar to
test_verified_chain_with_alternative_ca_cert() from connection.c, just
for GTlsFileDatabase rather than GTlsConnection. The idea is to ensure
we are able to build certification paths even if the root certificate
does not match, but the private key does. I first tried updating the
test, but ran into trouble, and decided it's not worth debugging. The
test is basically redundant with
test_verified_chain_with_alternative_ca_cert(). That test will fail if
this one would break. We can safely remove it.

Part-of: <https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib-networking/-/merge_requests/268>
---
 tls/tests/file-database.c                   | 104 --------------------
 tls/tests/files/ca-verisign-sha1.pem        |  48 ---------
 tls/tests/files/chain-with-verisign-md2.pem |  81 ---------------
 tls/tests/meson.build                       |   2 -
 4 files changed, 235 deletions(-)
 delete mode 100644 tls/tests/files/ca-verisign-sha1.pem
 delete mode 100644 tls/tests/files/chain-with-verisign-md2.pem

diff --git a/tls/tests/file-database.c b/tls/tests/file-database.c
