If no GTlsConnectionOpenSSL has been created before, and two different
threads create one at the same time, then the initialization races.
Fixing this is straightforward: do it in class init, so it only happens
once, rather than in instance init.

We don't need it at all in GTlsClientConnectionOpenSSL, so delete it.

This bug was spotted in #YWH-PGM9867-250, which I closed as spam because
it was submitted with a bogus proof of concept program. Shame, because
it's actually useful to get reports like these.
